  "notes": [
    "This is a PARISH-level congregational cycle -- the parish's own list of its individual members/households to pray for through the month -- not a diocese-level cycle of parishes. It is the first file in this corpus to use scope 'parish' and subject type 'household'. St. Bede's itself already appears as a diocese-level 'parish' subject in episcopal-western-oregon-2026.json (its own week, 2026-04-12, the file schema.json itself cites as this corpus's original precedent); this file is a different, finer-grained layer beneath that one -- the congregation praying for its own members, not the diocese praying for the congregation as a whole.",
    "The source's typographic '+' suffix after some names (Jane+, Ken+, Katheryn King+, Linda+, Daniel+) is preserved exactly as printed. It very likely denotes clergy (this parish's rector/associates), consistent with the 'Dcn.' prefix used elsewhere in the same document for deacons, but the source supplies no explicit key/legend, so its meaning is disclosed here rather than decoded or asserted.",
    "Each household/individual entry is transcribed exactly as printed, including however the source groups spouses ('&'), co-listed adults (comma-separated), and children (listed by first name only, comma-separated after the adult(s)) -- never split, re-ordered, or normalized.",
    "Day 31 is not a household at all -- the source lists parish ministries/outreach groups as a single comma-separated line ('St. Bede's Outreach Ministries, Relay for Life, Good News Pantry Garden, Eucharistic Visitors/Pastoral Care, Quilt & Prayer Shawl Ministry, Brotherhood at St. Bede's, Women's Fellowship, Christian Formation'). Each comma-separated item is recorded as its own 'category' subject (this corpus's existing type for a named group not tied to one individual/family), consistent with how diocesan-level files in this corpus already use 'category' for non-parish institutional subjects.",
    "The source PDF's raw copy-pasted text interleaves two printed columns into one run-on line for each pair of facing 'Day N' / 'Day N+7' boxes (e.g. 'Day 1 Day 8 Eva Alt Ron & Sue Field ...'). This file was transcribed from the PDF's own rendered page layout, not that linearized text extraction, specifically to avoid misassigning a name to the wrong day -- per the corresponding rule added to schema.json's own `rules` list."
  ],
